<jnt = 'http://www.jahia.org/jahia/nt/1.0'>
<jmix = 'http://www.jahia.org/jahia/mix/1.0'>
<ct = 'http://www.jahia.org/jahia/content-types/1.0'>

/**
 * Site level configuration for the Content Types accordion.
 *
 * Applied to the site node, so the choice belongs to the site rather than to a user, and everyone
 * working on that site sees the same list. An absent mixin, or an empty property, means no choice
 * has been made and every editorial type is listed: the configuration only ever narrows.
 */
[ct:contentTypesListing] mixin
 - ct:listedTypes (string) multiple

/**
 * What a task raised from the Content Types accordion is about.
 *
 * `jnt:task` carries a title, a description, an assignee and a state, but nothing that says which
 * content the task concerns - core only links a task to content on `jnt:workflowTask`, through a
 * `targetNode` that a plain task does not have. The content-review module answers the same gap the
 * same way, with a mixin of its own (`rvwmix:taskTarget`).
 *
 * Multiple, unlike content-review's, because a task raised here is raised from a selection: an
 * editor ticks the rows that need attention and describes the job once, so one task points at every
 * record it was raised for rather than the selection being split into one task each.
 *
 * A weak reference, so that deleting a record leaves the task standing rather than refusing the
 * deletion. A task outliving the content it named is a loose end somebody can close; content that
 * cannot be deleted because an old task mentions it is a problem with no way out.
 */
[ct:taskTarget] mixin
 - targetNode (weakreference) multiple
